  "task": {
    "objective": "Each skipper must touch its assigned buoy and then its distinct dock. Skippers receive own progress/arrival rewards and compete for the first-arrival bonus while towing can help a partner.",
    "natural_termination": "All three boats have arrived. A moored boat remains a stationary physical obstacle and has only action 0. Otherwise the time bound is 80 raw transitions.",
    "interaction": "A raised sail casts a length-two downwind shadow with crosswind width one, preventing nearby high-sail movement. Low sails row at a stamina cost. Voluntary low-sail recipients can be pulled into a helper old cell; the helper loses any second movement cell and one stamina. Occupancy, islands, buoy access and first-arrival timing create additional coupling.",
    "observation_access": "The terrain, buoy/dock locations, wind and clock are public. Another boat is visible exactly within Manhattan distance 3; its displayed attributes are present in the masked peer record. Own goal, sail, stamina and route state are always available. Tow entities are visible only when both endpoints are visible. Invisible data are zero with an explicit visibility bit; no privileged full state is a policy input."
  },
