  "action_resolution": "All nine intent actions are legal for unfinished boats; blocked, inapplicable or malformed actions deterministically have no effect or map to action 0. Directional actions on a currently towed recipient are suppressed while the link persists. Arrived boats and an absorbing terminal state allow only action 0. Sail/release changes precede shadow and tow allocation. New links use cyclic priority beginning at t mod 3 and lowest eligible recipient id. Normal movement cannot enter any other boat previous cell; duplicate proposed destinations cancel. Tow followers alone enter their helper vacated cell. A second downwind movement uses a new simultaneous occupancy check.",
  "rng_contract": "Reset fixes wind east and draws strength with jax.random.randint(reset_key,(1,),1,3,dtype=int32). Each nonterminal step splits its supplied key into two keys; wind direction index 0..3 and strength 1..2 are applied only when the new clock is divisible by six. Sailing uses the input-state wind; the newly sampled wind is the next-state wind. No hidden RNG, sampled route, seed remapping or key in state exists.",
  "event_visibility_note": "Per-step event arrays carry an explicit boat_visible binding. A role view may disclose only visible participants; full event arrays belong to a labelled debug view. No global arrival or tow event panel may reveal invisible boats.",
